<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RUGBY UNION-GERBER REPLACES MORDT AS SPRINGBOK SELECTOR.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-GERBER REPLACES MORDT AS SPRINGBOK SELECTOR.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Former Springbok full-back Mickey Gerber will replace Ray Mordt on South Africa's three-man national selection panel, SARFU announced on Friday.</p>
<p>Mordt resigned earlier this month after the surprise omission of former Springbok captain Francois Pienaar from the squad to tour Argentina, France and Wales later this year.</p>
<p>Gerber played three tests against France and Scotland in 1958 and 1960.</p>
</text>
